### name: re.ambiguity.reject.1
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a pattern a backtracking engine can be driven to exponential time on is refused at compile time, whatever the subject. (Patterns from the ReDoS literature and from real validation rules.) The subject is irrelevant; it is short on purpose so that only compile-time validation can produce the result.
--- source
RMATCH('(a+)+$', "aaa")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

