### name: re.ambiguity.flag-i.rejects.1
--- note
The `i` flag is folded into the analysis: the two branches are disjoint without it and overlap with it, so the same pattern is refused with `i` (the validator takes the flag; caches are keyed by it).
--- source
RMATCH('(?:a|A)+$', "aAa", "i")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.ambiguity.flag-i.accepts-without.1
--- note
CONTROL for the case before: without `i` the branches are disjoint and the pattern is fine.
--- source
RMATCH('(?:a|A)+$', "aAa")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

