### name: re.ambiguity.accept.1
--- note
A pattern that is NOT refused: real validation rules, patterns with polynomial (not exponential) ambiguity, and unambiguous alternations that share a prefix. A false rejection here would break working rules, so each is pinned. The expected match result comes from Python's re, not from SEL.
--- source
RMATCH('(\d+,)+', "12,3,")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

